    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-h/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The weekly mileages of a sales rep are thought to be Normally distributed with mean µ and standard deviation σ . 5% of his weekly mileages are less than 850 miles and 1% exceed 960 miles. ( ) 7 a) Find, correct to the nearest mile, the value of µ and the value of σ . The rep believes that the value of µ is much lower than the one found in part (a), based on a random sample of 4 weeks whose mean mileage was 863 . b) Using the value of σ found in part (a), conduct a hypothesis test at the 1% level of significance to investigate the rep&#x27;s belief. ( ) 6 State your hypotheses clearly.\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Putting the information in a diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:524.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The lower 5% and upper 1% cut-offs yield (850 −µ)/σ = Φ−1(0.05) ≈−1.64485, (960 −µ)/σ = Φ−1(0.99) ≈2.32635. [B1] [A1] Rearrange the two equations to µ = 850 + 1.64485σ and µ = 960 −2.32635σ. Equating them gives 3.97120σ = 110. Subtracting gives σ = 110/(2.32635 + 1.64485) ≈27.6994, [M1] [A1] and µ = 850 + 1.64485σ ≈895.5615. [A1] To the nearest mile, µ = 896, σ = 28 . [M1] [A1] (b) Test H0 : µ = 896 [B1] against H1 : µ &lt; 896, using the rounded σ = 28 [A1] from part (a). [A1] The sample mean of four weeks gives z = 863 −896 √ ≈−2.3571. [A1] 28/ 4\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q4-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The standard error is 28/2 = 14. In the critical-value method the lower 1% cutoff is −2.32635; the observed −2.3571 is further into that tail: The one-tailed p-value is about 0.00921 &lt; 0.01, so reject H0. [A1] There is evidence at 1% that the representative’s mean weekly mileage is lower than 896. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 13 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The weekly mileages of a sales rep are thought to be Normally distributed with mean µ and standard deviation σ . 5% of his weekly mileages are less than 850 miles and 1% exceed 960 miles. ( ) 7 a) Find, correct to the nearest mile, the value of µ and the value of σ . The rep believes that the value of µ is much lower than the one found in part (a), based on a random sample of 4 weeks whose mean mileage was 863 . b) Using the value of σ found in part (a), conduct a hypothesis test at the 1% level of significance to investigate the rep's belief. ( ) 6 State your hypotheses clearly. "
