    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A uniform rod AB has length 6 m and weight 40 kg . The rod rests in a horizontal position on two smooth supports at P and Q , where AP = 1 m and AQ = d m . The magnitude of the reaction force on the rod at Q is 3 times as large as that at P . Calculate the value of  d . ( ) 5\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Drawing a diagram: Let the reaction at P be R, then the reaction at Q is 3R. [M1] Forces balance vertically, so 4R = 40g [A1] and R = 10g. [A1] The vertical equation is R + 3R = 40g. With 3R = 30g, the moments equation reduces after division by g to 10 + 30d = 120, so 30d = 110.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Taking moments about A gives 10g(1) + 30gd = 40g(3), d = 11/3 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
