    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-h/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"100N θ 30° A particle of weight 120 N , rests on a smooth plane inclined at an angle of 30° to the horizontal. The box is kept in equilibrium by a force of magnitude 100 N , pushing at an angle of θ ( θ &gt; 30 ° to the direction of the greatest slope of the plane, as shown in the )\" style=\"--madas-width:558.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"above figure. Calculate the normal reaction between the particle and the plane. ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
