      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-h/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus cos θ = 0.6 [M1] [A1] and sin θ = 0.8. [A1] The reference triangle for cos θ = 3/5 has opposite side √ 52 −32 = 4. Hence sin θ = 4/5. Perpendicular to the plane, both the push and the weight have inward components: [A1] The reaction is √ R = 120 cos 30◦+ 100 sin θ = 60 3 + 80 ≈183.9 N . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
